Make extra AirPlay feature bits advertisable

Senders pick the AirPlay-picker icon like this (verified empirically
with synthetic mDNS registrations against iOS):

- Apple model strings map to product icons and win over feature bits
  (AudioAccessory5,1 / 1,1 / 6,1 and AppleTV models each have icons;
  AirPort, Mac, iPhone and RealityDevice models do not - they draw the
  plain generic speaker glyph in the audio picker).
- Otherwise bit 26 (Authentication_8, MFi) classifies the receiver as
  ThirdPartySpeaker (bookshelf icon; Sonos and WiiM advertise it), and
  bit 26 + bit 49 (SupportsAirPlayVideoV2) as ThirdPartyTV (TV icon).
  Bit 0 (video v1) does not trigger the TV classification.

shairport-sync hardcodes its features mask. New option:
general.airplay_features_or, a hex bitmask OR'd into the mask; default
unchanged. Companion to 0001 (general.airplay_device_model); carried
locally by boompi.

--- a/shairport.c	2026-08-06 02:40:48
+++ b/shairport.c	2026-08-06 16:20:00
@@ -595,6 +595,16 @@
       if (config_lookup_string(config.cfg, "general.airplay_device_model", &str)) {
         config.airplay_device_model = (char *)str;
       }
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_AIRPLAY_2
+      /* Extra AirPlay feature bits (hex, OR'd into the advertised mask).
+         Bit 26 (Authentication_8, MFi) draws the third-party bookshelf
+         speaker icon in senders' pickers; bits 26+49 draw the TV icon.
+         Apple model strings still take precedence over the bits. */
+      if (config_lookup_string(config.cfg, "general.airplay_features_or", &str)) {
+        config.airplay_features |= strtoull(str, NULL, 16);
+      }
+#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_LIBDAEMON
       /* Get the Daemonize setting. */
       config_set_lookup_bool(config.cfg, "sessioncontrol.daemonize_with_pid_file", &daemonisewith);
